From: =?utf-8?b?Ik1hcmNvIFRyZXZpc2FuIChUcmV2acOxbyki?= <mail@3v1n0.net>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 17:39:07 +0200
Subject: authServicesLegacy: Emit step-completed after each PAM request

GDM does notify us when a PAM request has been submitted and we got a
reply for it, also because there's really not a clear API for that.

The only way to be sure that a PAM service has completed the step is to
wait for a successive reply from the module.

So do this: as soon a request has been placed, track that and once we
got a reply, inform the auth prompt that the request has been
acknowledged by PAM
---
 js/gdm/authServicesLegacy.js | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/js/gdm/authServicesLegacy.js b/js/gdm/authServicesLegacy.js
index 12adc63..6c5f861 100644
--- a/js/gdm/authServicesLegacy.js
+++ b/js/gdm/authServicesLegacy.js
@@ -75,6 +75,15 @@ export class AuthServicesLegacy extends AuthServices {
         this.addCredentialManager(Vmware.SERVICE_NAME, Vmware.getVmwareCredentialsManager());
 
         this._fingerprintReadyTimeoutId = 0;
+        this._pendingSteps = new Set();
+    }
+
+    _maybeEmitStepCompleted(serviceName) {
+        if (!this._pendingSteps.has(serviceName))
+            return;
+
+        this.emit('step-completed', {serviceName});
+        this._pendingSteps.delete(serviceName);
     }
 
